<!-- ── § 04 — PROBLEM DEFINITION ── -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head">
    <span class="meta">§ 04 — Problem definition</span>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <h2 class="cs-h2">The features worked. The conditions didn't.</h2>
    <p class="body-text" style="font-size: 17px; max-width: 56ch;">
      Attendees wanted to connect — that was never the issue. What failed was the environment. Meaningful connection needs shared context, the right moment, and a reason that makes cold outreach feel worth the awkwardness. None of which existed naturally in a hybrid setting.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="gap-grid">
    <div class="gap">
      <div class="gap-num">Gap 01</div>
      <div class="gap-t">No shared context</div>
      <div class="gap-b">People knew who was there. They didn't know why it was worth saying hello.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="gap">
      <div class="gap-num">Gap 02</div>
      <div class="gap-t">No icebreaker</div>
      <div class="gap-b">There was nothing to break the ice — just a blank message field and a stranger's profile.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="gap">
      <div class="gap-num">Gap 03</div>
      <div class="gap-t">Hybrid friction</div>
      <div class="gap-b">The right tool wasn't available at the right moment, onsite or online.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


