<!-- ── § 07 — TAKEAWAYS ── -->
<section class="section-alt">
  <div class="section-head">
    <span class="meta">§ 07 — Takeaways</span>
  </div>
  <h2 class="cs-h2-wide">What this project taught me.</h2>

  <div class="takeaway-grid">
    <div class="takeaway">
      <div class="takeaway-num">01</div>
      <div class="takeaway-t">Context before capability</div>
      <div class="takeaway-b">The most powerful space in the product was barely used, not because of usability, but because the conditions to use it weren't there.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway">
      <div class="takeaway-num">02</div>
      <div class="takeaway-t">Research should precede the brief</div>
      <div class="takeaway-b">The framework we ended up with came from watching where the experience broke, not from assumptions made upfront.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway">
      <div class="takeaway-num">03</div>
      <div class="takeaway-t">Hybrid is a social design problem</div>
      <div class="takeaway-b">The challenge wasn't technical. It was reducing the cost of reaching out across a divide that was partly physical, partly psychological.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


